    "result_text": "All 47 tests pass. The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `birthDate` \u2192 `ageBand` feature on `POST /api/owners`, following the codebase's established pattern of read-time derived fields (like `membershipLevel`, `locality`, `contactPreference`).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`**\n   - Added `birthDate` (optional, `format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` request schema.\n   - Added `ageBand` (read-only string) to the `Owner` response schema.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`**\n   - Added a persisted `birthDate` field (`@Column(name = \"birth_date\")`) with getter/setter.\n   - Added a `@Transient getAgeBand()` that computes the band from `birthDate` measured against `registrationDate` using `Period.between(...).getYears()`: `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), `SENIOR` (65+), returning `null` when `birthDate` (or `registrationDate`) is absent.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added a `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table.\n\nNo pipeline or mapper changes were needed: MapStruct maps `birthDate` (request\u2192entity) and `ageBand`/`birthDate` (entity\u2192response) by name automatically, and `ageBand` is computed at read time against the already-defaulted/business-day-adjusted `registrationDate`.\n\nThe new `Cp34Tests` (birthDate `1990-01-01` \u2192 `ADULT`) passes, and all 47 acceptance tests remain green.",
